"""Original governance scenarios; all requirements and figures are hypothetical."""
ITEMS=[]
def family(options, rows):
    assert len(options)==len(rows)==4
    for k,(stem,why) in enumerate(rows):
        ITEMS.append((stem,[options[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(options) if j!=k],why))
family(['Map obligations to controls','Assign decision ownership','Reconcile the asset inventory','Approve an exception expiry'],[
('A merger leaves two control catalogs covering the same contractual requirements. Auditors cannot tell which evidence satisfies which requirement. Which governance action directly resolves this traceability gap?', 'Mapping each obligation to controls and evidence resolves traceability. Assigning ownership helps execution but does not establish coverage.'),
('Two executives each assume the other can accept a critical residual risk. The mitigation work is already funded and tracked. Which governance action addresses the unresolved authority?', 'Explicit decision ownership identifies who may accept the risk. An inventory or control mapping does not confer that authority.'),
('Cloud billing lists twelve production subscriptions, while the configuration database lists nine. The security team cannot establish the population for its control review. What should it do first?', 'Reconcile discovery and billing with the inventory before assessing coverage. Otherwise three subscriptions may remain outside the review.'),
('A legacy service cannot meet a required configuration until a signed replacement contract completes. The risk owner permits temporary compensating controls, but the exception has no review boundary. What should be added?', 'An approved expiry or review date prevents an exception from silently becoming permanent. The temporary acceptance still requires documented controls and ownership.')])
family(['Measure the current outcomes','Define the desired outcomes','Prioritize the identified gaps','Verify the completed changes'],[
('A company begins a CSF profile exercise. It has a list of desired capabilities but no reliable evidence of which outcomes it achieves today. Which activity supplies the missing baseline?', 'A Current Profile records achieved outcomes and supporting status. A Target Profile alone cannot establish the starting point.'),
('A hospital has assessed its present security posture and now plans a remote-care service with new dependencies. What profile activity should capture the security outcomes needed for that future service?', 'The Target Profile expresses desired outcomes, including anticipated changes. Current-state measurement documents what exists now.'),
('A retailer has agreed Current and Target Profiles. It has enough budget for only three of twelve differences this quarter. What is the next planning activity?', 'Risk-informed gap prioritization turns the comparison into an actionable plan. Repeating the baseline does not allocate the scarce budget.'),
('A business reports that every action in its CSF improvement plan is closed. Before updating the Current Profile to show the target achieved, what should the assessor do?', 'Verify that the changes actually produce the intended outcomes. Completed tickets are not, by themselves, evidence of effectiveness.')])
family(['Establish a supplier baseline','Assess a new subprocessor','Exercise joint incident duties','Revoke access at termination'],[
('Procurement is about to invite bids for a hosted payroll platform. No vendor has been selected, and bidders need comparable minimum security expectations. Which action belongs at this point?', 'Define baseline supplier requirements before selection so proposals can be evaluated consistently. A later joint exercise cannot replace procurement criteria.'),
('An approved cloud vendor announces that a new company will process customer records in another jurisdiction. Existing service features remain unchanged. Which action targets the new risk?', 'A changed subprocessor creates new access and jurisdiction dependencies that require assessment. The original vendor approval does not automatically cover that change.'),
('A critical outsourcing contract names internal and vendor incident contacts, but neither team has tested escalation or evidence handoff. Which activity most directly checks whether those arrangements work?', 'A joint exercise tests cross-organizational incident responsibilities. Contract wording or a baseline alone does not demonstrate execution.'),
('A support agreement has ended and all required records have been returned. The supplier still has a federated support account. Which lifecycle action closes this remaining exposure?', 'Termination should remove obsolete supplier access. An assessment of a future supplier would not remove the existing credential path.')])
family(['Accept the documented exposure','Reduce the event likelihood','Transfer the financial impact','Discontinue the risky service'],[
('A risk owner reviews a low-impact exposure already within approved tolerance. Further controls would cost more than the expected benefit, and no binding requirement is unmet. Which response fits this decision?', 'Documented acceptance is appropriate when authorized and within tolerance. Acceptance is a deliberate risk decision, not an undocumented omission.'),
('A business keeps a needed remote service but deploys phishing-resistant authentication to make account takeover less likely. Which risk response describes this change?', 'The control mitigates risk by reducing event likelihood. It does not shift financial loss to another party.'),
('A company retains its service and existing controls but purchases coverage for specified incident-related losses. Which response describes the insurance arrangement?', 'Insurance transfers specified financial consequences under its terms. It does not remove the threat or transfer all accountability.'),
('An organization decides that a proposed biometric feature creates unacceptable residual privacy risk and removes the feature from its product plan. Which response is this?', 'Eliminating the activity avoids its associated risk. Mitigation would retain the activity with controls.')])
family(['Compare quantified loss estimates','Rank defined impact bands','Test the recovery capability','Validate the control evidence'],[
('A board asks which of two investments yields the greater expected annual reduction in monetary loss. Reliable frequency and cost estimates are available. Which analysis best answers its question?', 'Quantitative comparison estimates losses and investment effects in monetary terms. Qualitative bands do not provide the requested monetary comparison.'),
('An emerging threat has too little reliable frequency data for defensible monetary estimates. Stakeholders can consistently distinguish limited, serious and catastrophic mission effects. Which assessment approach fits?', 'Defined qualitative bands support ranking without invented numerical precision. Recovery testing addresses a narrower operational question.'),
('A risk register assumes the billing service can be restored inside its agreed outage limit. Backup jobs complete, but nobody has restored the service. Which action tests the assumption?', 'A recovery exercise measures restoration capability. Successful backup creation alone does not establish recoverability.'),
('A mitigation owner marks an access-review finding resolved. The assessor needs assurance that excess privileges were actually removed. Which action provides the relevant evidence?', 'Validation checks the resulting access state against the requirement. Recalculating loss estimates does not prove the control was implemented.')])
family(['Preserve the held records','Apply the retention schedule','Restrict the processing purpose','Review cross-border obligations'],[
('Counsel issues a valid legal hold covering specified investigation records. The normal deletion job will reach those records tonight. Which action should the information owner arrange?', 'Preserve the records subject to the hold while coordinating with counsel. Routine retention deletion must not destroy material covered by the hold.'),
('A dataset reaches its approved retention limit. Counsel confirms there is no hold or other retention duty, and the business has no remaining authorized purpose. Which action follows lifecycle governance?', 'Apply the approved disposal schedule after checking overriding obligations. Indefinite retention adds exposure without a justified purpose.'),
('A team proposes using identifiable support records for unrelated model training. The records remain within the same country, but the new purpose has not been assessed or authorized. What should governance address first?', 'The proposed new processing purpose needs review and restriction until authorized. Keeping data in one country does not resolve purpose and privacy concerns.'),
('A regional service will move personal records to a foreign processor. The same processing purpose continues. Which issue needs specific review before the move?', 'Cross-border obligations depend on the applicable jurisdictions and transfer arrangements. An unchanged purpose does not eliminate those requirements.')])
family(['Trace the data and trust boundaries','Enumerate the relevant threat paths','Select risk-reducing safeguards','Retest the revised design'],[
('Design reviewers cannot explain where an external analytics provider receives customer records or which identity crosses into its service. Which threat-modeling activity is missing?', 'Modeling flows and trust boundaries establishes what is being protected and where trust changes. Threat selection needs that context.'),
('A team has a complete architecture model and now asks how an adversary could reach the protected transaction service through its dependencies. Which activity answers that question?', 'Threat-path enumeration explores ways the modeled system could be abused. Merely documenting existing controls would skip threat identification.'),
('Reviewers have identified a credible attack path through a partner integration and agreed its risk is unacceptable. What threat-modeling activity should follow?', 'Select and design mitigations for the identified risk, then validate them. Repeating discovery alone does not address the agreed exposure.'),
('A new isolation boundary has been added to close a documented threat path. Which activity determines whether the threat model can treat that path as mitigated?', 'Validation tests the changed design against the threat. A planned safeguard is not evidence that the attack path is closed.')])
family(['Limit the assistant permissions','Validate downstream model output','Control training-data provenance','Require human decision review'],[
('A purchasing assistant can both recommend vendors and execute unrestricted purchases. The immediate concern is excessive agency even when its recommendations are accurate. Which safeguard most directly reduces this exposure?', 'Constrain tool permissions and allowed actions to the assistant’s legitimate role. Reviewing output format alone does not restrict execution authority.'),
('A model returns structured content that another service treats as trusted instructions. Tool permissions are already narrow, but malformed output can alter that service’s behavior. Which boundary needs a control?', 'Treat model output as untrusted and validate it before downstream use. Narrow permissions do not make every permitted input safe.'),
('A model’s behavior changes after unverified third-party records are added to its training corpus. Which process most directly addresses the suspected supply of poisoned material?', 'Training-data provenance and review target the source of poisoning. Human review of isolated final decisions does not repair the data pipeline.'),
('A benefits system gives a model’s recommendation final authority over consequential eligibility decisions. The policy requires an accountable reviewer to assess evidence and exceptions. Which safeguard satisfies that requirement?', 'Meaningful human decision review addresses overreliance in a consequential workflow. Output-schema validation only checks structure.')])
family(['An indirect prompt injection','An unauthorized model disclosure','An availability resource attack','A training-data integrity attack'],[
('An enterprise assistant retrieves a supplier page containing instructions that conflict with its assigned task. It follows those page instructions. Which AI threat category best describes the entry path?', 'The instructions arrived through external retrieved content, making this indirect prompt injection. The scenario does not describe a changed training corpus.'),
('A protected model artifact is copied by a contractor without authorization. There is no evidence of altered training or service interruption. Which category best describes the observed loss?', 'Unauthorized copying of the model is a confidentiality loss affecting the model itself. Data poisoning would change the training input.'),
('Monitoring shows deliberately expensive model requests saturating inference capacity and preventing ordinary users from receiving responses. Which category best describes the effect?', 'The requests exhaust service resources, causing an availability attack. Incorrect training labels are a different integrity issue.'),
('Before a model is trained, an attacker systematically changes labels in a trusted training dataset. Which category best describes the compromise?', 'Changing training labels compromises training-data integrity. Prompt injection instead uses instructions presented during model interaction.')])
family(['Reassess the residual risk','Escalate beyond delegated authority','Implement the approved treatment','Retire a superseded risk entry'],[
('A completed control materially reduces the probability of a recorded threat, but the register still shows the pre-control exposure. Which update is needed before the next acceptance decision?', 'Reassess residual risk using the new control state. Treatment completion does not automatically mean the remaining risk is acceptable.'),
('A project manager may accept exposures up to the company’s moderate band. The assessed residual risk is high, and the service is still required. Which governance step is needed?', 'Escalation to an authorized risk owner respects the defined authority boundary. The project manager cannot accept a higher band merely because delivery is urgent.'),
('An authorized risk owner has approved a funded mitigation plan with named owners and dates. The team has not yet applied the control. What is the immediate next step?', 'Execute the approved treatment, then validate its effect. Repeatedly requesting the same decision does not reduce the exposure.'),
('A system has been decommissioned and its records disposed of lawfully. Review confirms that a threat entry relates only to that system, with no remaining dependencies. What should the register owner do?', 'Close or retire the obsolete entry with evidence and history preserved. Keeping it active distorts the current risk picture.')])
family(['A policy-level requirement','A mandatory technical standard','An operational procedure','A nonbinding implementation guide'],[
('Leadership states that sensitive customer information must be protected throughout its lifecycle and assigns organizational accountability. Which documentation layer expresses this broad direction?', 'A policy establishes management direction and obligations. Technical settings belong in supporting standards.'),
('An organization specifies an approved minimum configuration that every managed server must meet unless an exception is granted. Which documentation type fits this mandatory baseline?', 'A standard makes the technical baseline mandatory. A guideline is advisory rather than an enforceable minimum.'),
('An on-call runbook identifies the ordered steps, approval checks and rollback actions for rotating a service credential. Which documentation type is this?', 'A procedure explains how to execute a defined task. A policy states intent without the same operational sequence.'),
('A security team publishes optional examples of useful dashboard layouts. Teams may choose alternatives without requesting an exception. Which documentation type fits?', 'Nonbinding guidance provides recommendations and examples. A mandatory standard would require compliance or an approved exception.')])
family(['Test the communications plan','Check the evidence preservation plan','Review the business recovery order','Confirm the decision delegation'],[
('A crisis exercise reveals that staff receive conflicting public statements because several departments brief the media independently. Which plan element needs focused testing?', 'A coordinated communications plan defines audiences, channels and authorized messages. Recovery order does not resolve inconsistent statements.'),
('During a breach exercise, responders overwrite relevant records while rebuilding systems. Which plan element needs correction to support later investigation?', 'Evidence preservation must be integrated with response and recovery. Communications coordination alone does not protect artifacts.'),
('A recovery drill restores a reporting service before the identity service it requires, delaying all usable access. Which planning element should be revised?', 'Recovery sequencing must reflect business criticality and technical dependencies. A nominal restoration that cannot function does not meet the business objective.'),
('A simulated incident occurs while the primary executive is unavailable. No participant knows who can authorize an emergency service shutdown. What governance element is missing?', 'Delegated authority and alternates let necessary decisions be made during absences. Contact lists alone do not grant decision rights.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==48
